<title>USA: St. Jude Medical, Ventritex sued.</title>
<headline>St. Jude Medical, Ventritex sued.</headline>
<dateline>ST. PAUL, Minn. 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>St. Jude Medical Inc and Ventritex Inc said Wednesday they received copies of complaints filed by Guidant Corp and Eli Lilly and Co against St. Jude, its wholly owned Pacesetter Inc subsidiary, Teletronics Pacing Systems Inc and Ventritex.</p>
<p>The complaints, filed in state and federal courts in Indiana, allege that St. Jude's previously announced agreements to acquire the cardiac rhythm management assets of Telectronics Group and Ventritex violate Guidant's licensing rights.</p>
</text>
